{"study_accession":"PRJNA525651","secondary_study_accession":"SRP187551","title":"Increase in innate lymphoid cells during acute ST-segment elevated myocardial infarction and its clinical relevance","description":"Purpose: Next-generation sequencing (NGS) has revolutionized systems-based analysis of cellular pathways. The goals of this study are to use RNA-seq to compare ILC1s gene expression in ST segmment elevation myocardial infarction patient compared with healthy control. Results: Using an optimized data analysis workflow, More than 70 million clean reads were obtained from each sample group after elimination of low-quality reads. A total of 4204 DEGs were found up-regulated and 4712 DEGs down-regulated on comparison of ILC1s from STEMI patients and controls. Conclusion: The dynamic number and gene expression changes in the subtype ILC1s indicate the role of ILCs in STEMI. Overall design: Methods: ILC1s mRNA profiles of STEMI patients and those of control were generated by deep sequencing, using Hiseq Xten . The sequence reads that passed quality filters were analyzed at the transcript isoform level with two methods: Burrows–Wheeler Aligner (BWA) followed by ANOVA (ANOVA) and TopHat followed by Cufflinks.","pubmed":"32198366","geo_series":"","n_samples":6,"study_labels":[{"level":"study","event_code":"MYOCARDIAL_INFARCTION","certainty":"history","delta_days":-60.0,"delta_bucket":"B_FAR","time_precision":"approx","stage":"teacher","confidence":1.0,"evidence":"Increase in innate lymphoid cells during acute ST-segment elevated myocardial infarction and its clinical relevance","model_version":"teacher:mlx:mlx-community/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-4bit"},{"level":"study","event_code":"MYOCARDIAL_INFARCTION","certainty":"history","delta_days":-60.0,"delta_bucket":"B_FAR","time_precision":"approx","stage":"teacher","confidence":1.0,"evidence":"The goals of this study are to use RNA-seq to compare ILC1s gene expression in ST segmment elevation myocardial infarction patient co